00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:04.550 align:start position:0%
stratford-on-avon district council is  currently consulting on a site  allocations plan and we want to hear  your views  to help explain what it's all about this  short video explains part of the plan  that relates to reserve housing sites  essentially what they are why we need  them as well as how we've identified  them  our existing plan the core strategy is  delivering the homes that this district  needs  however there's always the risk that  some of the sites already identified  do not actually get built or that  additional needs for housing arise  for this reason the site allocations  plan proposes reserve housing sites that  the council will release for development  if necessary  there there is a safety net if required  chapter 2 and policies sap 1 to sap 5  relate to reserve  sites there are 4 reasons why we are  identifying reserve  sites the first is to help us maintain a  5-year supply of housing  as we are required to do by the  government our latest figures show that  we have the equivalent of seven years  worth of supply  which is really good news the second  reason  relates to additional jobs being created  by jaguar land rover at gaiden lighthorn  heath  these new workers will need homes to  live in  the third and fourth reason relates to  additional housing needs arising outside  of the district  for example in birmingham or coventry we  have to do our bit to meet any such  shortfalls because we're in the same  housing market area  so have we identified the proposed  reserve sites  firstly we have applied the approach  already established in the core strategy  which identifies stratford-upon-avon as  the main town  eight main rural centres including  ulster bidford and southam  and four categories of local service  villages  secondly we have assessed the sites  against a range of technical criteria  including flood risk highways and  heritage  all this technical information is  available on the website at  www.stratford.gov  dot uk forward slash sappo  we have not identified reserve housing  sites in the greenvale or in the  cotswold aomb  all of the sites proposed will have  impacts and none are completely free  from constraints but we think on balance  the sites proposed are potentially  suitable  this is why we're consulting to hear  your views  are also proposing that developers of  reserve sites meet much more stringent  low-carbon requirements to help  combat climate change the proposed  reserve housing sites are listed in  annex 1 of the preferred options version  of the site allocations plan  and are also shown on the maps in part a  of chapter eight  more detailed site performers  identifying how site-specific  constraints should be overcome  are included in annex 2. i hope that's  helped and that you're now a little more  clued in as to why we need reserve sites  and how we've identified them  remember to find out more and to have  your say go to www.stratford.gov  dot uk forward slash sapo
 

